# §7 — DI service/svc with IService synthesis; Path-2 runtime-key resolved inline (no locator, no crash)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT SAILED (surface only; old annotation DI still present, retired in the next reseed):
#   - GRAMMAR: `service` is a KIND in `type Name = <kind>` (like class/struct/interface), with a
#     lifetime modifier `singleton`/`scoped`/`transient` (`type Clock = service singleton { … }`);
#     `TokenKind::Service`; `parse_service_body`/`parse_service_lifetime`; `ClassBody.is_service` +
#     `ServiceLifetime`. A `virtual`/`abstract service` is rejected (a service is always sealed).
#   - IService: the compiler SYNTHESIZES `exp type IService = interface { exp static ctor(): self }`
#     (root-visible); every `service` auto-conforms (its `static ctor(): self` factory satisfies it).
#     Two interface-contract capabilities were taught: a STATIC method contract, and `self` as a
#     contract's return type (bound to the conforming type in `method_sig_matches`). `type_satisfies_
#     iservice` gates the intrinsics: satisfied by a concrete `service` OR an `interface & IService`.
#   - `svc<T: IService>(key: str | null = null): T` and `has_svc<T: IService>(key: str): bool`,
#     recognized in `type_call` by callee shape. The CHECKER's type table IS the service registry —
#     there is NO second codegen-side registry, so the dual-registry OOB that crashed the lost
#     implementation cannot recur. A const/by-type key resolves to the concrete `Provider::ctor()`
#     inline; a RUNTIME key lowers to an INLINE if-chain (`if key=="A" { A::ctor() } else … else
#     panic`) typed as T, each arm upcast by the ordinary `emit_as` — no locator function, no vtable
#     enumeration. A PLAIN interface (not `& IService`) is a clean type error, never a crash.
#   - Escape rule keys on PROVENANCE (a value obtained from `svc<T>()`), not on service TYPE — a
#     freshly-constructed value returned from the `ctor` factory (an ordinary static method) is fine.
#   - const-key miss = compile-time error; runtime-key miss = `tk_panic` (guarded by `has_svc`);
#     same-type-same-key registration = compile-time error.
#   - `.tkb`: `ClassBody` carries `is_service`/`service_lifetime`; `TKB_EXPR_VERSION` 3→4,
#     `TKB_PROGRAM_VERSION` 5→6. NO runtime C touched. The per-thread arena-slot placement stays the
#     Doc 1 §8 SEAM (`svc_scope_expr`); today the lowering is simplest-correct (fresh build via `ctor`).
